{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Heat shrink tubing would help finish electrical repairs using my wire connectors, so it has a concrete use alongside supplies I already bought.",
    "Repair adhesives fit my tape and vinyl cement purchases. The small Gorilla epoxy feels especially suitable for an occasional repair, and my previous Gorilla purchases make it familiar."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Cutting wheels, locking nuts and a caliper require specific jobs or equipment that my purchases do not establish I need now.",
    "Neither thermometer addresses a task I have shown a need for, and electrical connectors alone do not give me a reason to buy electronic cleaner.",
    "Twelve tubes of super glue feel excessive. J-B Weld interests me as a repair adhesive, but I would choose the small Gorilla syringe this time."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any workshop supply, when I choose things for particular repair tasks.",
    "Buying electrical connectors seems to have been stretched into needing electronic maintenance products, although insulating a connection and cleaning components are different jobs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I value supplies that complete a task suggested by something I already bought, such as insulation for my wire connectors.",
    "Quantity matters for the particular supply: I have bought assortments and bulk tape, but that does not mean I need twelve tubes of glue.",
    "My repeated Gorilla tape purchases make Gorilla epoxy appealing to try, but a clear repair use still matters more than familiarity alone."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognized my practical repair interests but often assumed specific projects where only a broad connection existed."
}"}
